---
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// Placeholder image since local asset is missing
const blogHero =
    "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486406146926-c627a92ad1ab?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2070&ixlib=rb-4.0.3";
---

<MainLayout
    title="The Template Trap: Why 'quick and easy' ends up being very expensive | Otterock Blog"
    description="Discover why cheap is expensive when choosing generic templates"
    image={blogHero}
    type="article"
    articleData={{
        publishedTime: "2026-02-02",
        authorName: "Sergio Bello",
        section: "Web Strategy",
        tags: ["Technical Debt", "WordPress", "Performance", "Scalability"],
    }}
>
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-6">
        <header class="mb-12 text-center">
            <a
                href="/en/blog"
                class="inline-block mb-8 text-sm text-otter-deep font-bold hover:text-otter-accent transition-colors hover:underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                ← Back to Blog
            </a>

            <span
                class="text-slate-600 font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-xs mb-4 block font-body"
            >
                Web Strategy • 5 min read
            </span>

            <h1
                class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-6 leading-tight font-display"
            >
                The Template Trap: Why "quick and easy" ends up being very expensive
            </h1>

            <div
                class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-12 aspect-video bg-otter-deep relative"
            >
                <img
                    src={blogHero}
                    alt="Modern architecture representing solid structure"
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-90"
                    loading="eager"
                />
            </div>

            <!-- GEO Optimization: Key Takeaways (TL;DR) -->
            <div
                class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 rounded-2xl p-8 text-left mb-12"
            >
                <h2
                    class="text-lg font-black text-otter-deep uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 flex items-center gap-2"
                >
                    <span class="text-2xl">💡</span> Key Takeaways (TL;DR)
                </h2>
                <ul
                    class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 list-disc list-inside font-medium font-body"
                >
                    <li>
                        <strong>Cheap is expensive:</strong> Templates save money today 
                        but generate technical debt and limit growth tomorrow.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>"Bloated" Code:</strong> All-in-one solutions load 
                        thousands of unnecessary lines, slowing down your site.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Compromised security:</strong> An excess of plugins 
                        is the favorite entry point for hackers.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Generic identity:</strong> Your unique brand deserves 
                        more than the same design used by thousands of other businesses.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-body">
            <p
                class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-bold first-letter:text-otter-deep first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:float-left"
            >
                When you start a business, the temptation is huge. You see an ad 
                that says: "Create your website in 5 minutes, without knowing how 
                to code, drag and drop". Sounds perfect, right? For a few dollars a 
                month, you have something that looks professional. But after a few 
                months, the problems begin. Welcome to the <strong>Template Trap</strong>.
            </p>

            <p>
                At <strong>Otterock</strong>, we believe there is a big difference 
                between renting decorations and building a structure. Today we 
                explain why choosing the easy path can be the most costly mistake 
                for your brand.
            </p>

            <section>
                <h2
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                >
                    1. The "All in One" Problem (Junk Code)
                </h2>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    Imagine you're going for a light hike and you buy a backpack. 
                    But that backpack mandatorily comes with a tent, a stove, three 
                    sleeping bags, and an electric generator sewn inside. You can't 
                    take them out. You have to carry all that weight even if you only 
                    wanted to store a bottle of water.
                </p>
                <p>
                    That's how WordPress and generic templates work. To serve everyone 
                    (the baker, the lawyer, and the hotel), they bring thousands of 
                    lines of code that your business DOES NOT need.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-4 pl-4 space-y-2">
                    <li>
                        <strong>The result:</strong> An obese and slow website.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>The Otterock solution:</strong> We use <em>Handcrafted Code</em>. 
                        We write line by line only what your project needs. If your 
                        website were an athlete, it would have 0% body fat.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                >
                    2. The Plugin Nightmare (Paper Security)
                </h2>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    In the template world, if you want to add a function, you have to 
                    install a "Plugin". Soon you have 20 pieces of software from 
                    different creators trying to work together. It's a ticking time bomb. 
                    Plugins become outdated, open security holes, and are the favorite 
                    entry point for hackers.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Our web applications, built with modern technologies like 
                    <strong>Astro</strong>, don't rely on this house of cards. They 
                    are solid, closed, and secure structures.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                >
                    3. The Twin Syndrome
                </h2>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    Have you ever entered a website and felt a sense of "déjà vu"? 
                    That's because thousands of businesses use the same template as you. 
                    If you sell unique experiences (like luxury Glamping), luxury is 
                    exclusivity.
                </p>
                <div
                    class="bg-otter-sand/50 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-otter-deep my-6 italic text-slate-800"
                >
                    A template tells your client: "I'm just one of the crowd". 
                    Custom development tells them: "I'm unique".
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                >
                    4. Technical Debt: The glass ceiling
                </h2>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    Platforms like Wix or Squarespace are excellent... until you want 
                    to grow. The day you need a specific function that the platform 
                    doesn't offer, you'll hit a wall. You're trapped by their rules.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12"
                >
                    Conclusion: Expense or Investment?
                </h2>
                <p class="mb-4">
                    A template is cheap today, but you pay for it with lost clients 
                    and technical frustration tomorrow. Custom development is a larger 
                    initial investment, yes. But it is your property, optimized to sell 
                    for years and with the guarantee that Google will find a perfect 
                    piece of engineering.
                </p>
                <p class="font-bold text-otter-deep">
                    At Otterock, we don't use molds. We sculpt your digital presence 
                    so that it fits perfectly with the greatness of your business.
                </p>
            </section>

            <!-- E-E-A-T: Author Bio -->
            <footer class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-slate-200">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
                    <div
                        class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-otter-deep flex items-center justify-center text-3xl shrink-0 overflow-hidden"
                    >
                        👨‍💻
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <p
                            class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1"
                        >
                            Written by
                        </p>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep">
                            Sergio Bello
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-1 max-w-lg">
                            Director & Lead Developer. Specialist in creating 
                            scalable and high-performance digital architectures.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </footer>
        </div>
    </article>
</MainLayout>
